    <briefdescription>
<para>Driver for the TI TPSM8286x step-down power module with I2C (PMBus-style) output voltage control. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Bus-agnostic core driver: it only uses injected HAL callbacks (<ref refid="tpsm8286x_8h_1a42ab45a189add9f0a7df545e0aeacdc1" kindref="member">tpsm8286_i2c_write_f</ref> / <ref refid="tpsm8286x_8h_1abad7796fa9cc625c12cf89fc1fc95a84" kindref="member">tpsm8286_i2c_read_f</ref>), never a concrete I2C driver directly. The callback signatures match <ref refid="i2cWrapper_8c_1afa738982ab2a9c744b4c07f67db541af" kindref="member">i2c_writeReg()</ref>/i2c_readReg() in <ref refid="i2cWrapper_8h" kindref="compound">drivers/i2c/i2cWrapper.h</ref>, so they can be passed directly via a function-pointer cast.</para>
<para>Multiple simultaneous instances are supported: <ref refid="tpsm8286x_8h_1a275328fffd1fae5d932dfcbe6cf6d541" kindref="member">tpsm8286_initialize()</ref> takes an explicit <computeroutput>devId</computeroutput> that indexes the static instance pool (size <ref refid="userDef_8h_1a6d2ebc133d3d6b30e585478b8488101b" kindref="member">TPSM8286_NUM_OF_INSTANCES</ref>, defined in <ref refid="userDef_8h" kindref="compound">userDef.h</ref>). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
